<title>UK: Bulker aground at Saudi port with 33,988 T barley.</title>
<headline>Bulker aground at Saudi port with 33,988 T barley.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulk carrier Qena is aground in the approach to Dammam port in Saudi Arabia with a cargo of 33,988 tonnes of bulk barley, Lloyds Shipping Intelligence Service said.</p>
<p>The Egyptian-flag 38,319 dwt vessel ran aground two days ago. Part of the cargo may have to be discharged before the vessel can be refloated, Lloyds said.</p>
<p>Qena sailed from Albany, Wa. for the Gulf on January 7.</p>
</text>
